  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in West Virginia are $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Award activity in FY2026 to date includes 3,867 awards with an average award size of $314K. Obligations fell 35.2% year over year. Annual obligations peaked at $2B in FY24 and then fell to $1.9B in FY25 and to $1.2B in FY26 to date. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date at $264M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $226M and the Department of Justice at $209M. Other large buying agencies include the Department of Defense at $150M and the Department of the Treasury at $135M. Other Computer Related Services is the largest industry by obligations at $164M, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $157M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $131M. LEIDOS, INC. is the largest vendor in FY2026 to date at $125M, followed by SAWTOOTH CONSTRUCTION JV II LLC at $60.7M and IMPRES TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, INC at $50.5M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 35.2% year over year. Annual obligations moved from $2B in FY24 to $1.9B in FY25 and to $1.2B in FY26 to date. The number of awards in FY2026 to date is 3,867 with an average award size of $314K. These figures show a lower current-year total compared with the prior two fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and industries in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the top buying agency at $264M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $226M and the Department of Justice at $209M. The Department of Defense obligated $150M and the Department of the Treasury obligated $135M in FY2026 to date. Other Computer Related Services is the top industry at $164M, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $157M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $131M."
      }
    ]
  },
